/T (In light of recent developments regarding the security of sats, we've clearly not realized this. People saying "I've done everything right, yet I lost my entire stack" is evidence that what consensus \(per sentiment, consensus = the tweeter/podcast sphere\) says is right, doesn't have to actually be right and the consequence is unmitigated vulnerability. After all, an unmitigated vulnerability in software that you run becomes your vulnerability: you inherit it.)
/E (In light of recent developments regarding the security of sats, we've clearly not realized this. People saying "I've done everything right, yet I lost my entire stack" is evidence that what consensus \(per sentiment, consensus = the tweeter/podcast sphere\) says is right, doesn't have to actually be right and the consequence is unmitigated vulnerability. After all, an unmitigated vulnerability in software that you run becomes your vulnerability: you inherit it.)
